WEBVTT


00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.700
<i>Friendship between Austria</i>
<i>and France...</i>


00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.000
<i>...must be cemented by marriage.</i>


00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.600
<i>My youngest daughter, Antoine...</i>


00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.700
<i>...will be queen of France.</i>


00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.900
Mops.


00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.900
The court of France
is not like Vienna.


00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:24.000
Listen closely to
Ambassador Mercy's council.


00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.300
All eyes will be on you.


00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.900
Look.


00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.900
Do you like him?


00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.000
He has kind eyes.


00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.600
He's definitely very French.


00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.900
- Three. Four.
- Six.


00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.500
Are we there yet?


00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.300
Yes, we have arrived at Schüttern for
the official handover.


00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:43.100
Then you will be presented to the king
and to your fiancé, Louis Auguste.


00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.400
Your Royal Highness, may I present
your mistress of the household...


00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.800
...Comtesse de Noailles.


00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.000
Your Royal Highness.


00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.200
Madame.


00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.100
This structure for
the handover ceremony...


00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:23.600
...has been built precisely astride
the borders of the two great lands.


00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.300
You have entered on Austrian soil...


00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.000
...you will exit on French
as the dauphine of France.


00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.300
Now you must bid farewell
to your party...


00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.100
...and leave all of Austria behind.


00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.500
Goodbye.


00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.100
Mops.


00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.500
You can have as many
French dogs as you like.


00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.200
It is a custom...


00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:27.100
...that the bride retain nothing
belonging to a foreign court.


00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.000
An etiquette always observed
on such an occasion.


00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.600
You're lucky.
Apparently she's quite beautiful.


00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.900
I'll probably end up with someone
who looks like a dog.


00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.400
- Or a horse.
- Or a horse.


00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.800
I've heard she's really nice.


00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:49.900
- Think they got rabbits here?
- Maybe.


00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.100
Come on.


00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.500
You notice anything strange
about me lately?


00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.600
It's so muddy here.


00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:07.400
I know. My stomach feels
a little bit sick.


00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.700
Are you feeling better now?
Are you feeling better, Camille?


00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.700
- I wonder if our little doggie is sick.
- Feel a little sickly.


00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.500
Now.


00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.300
Oh, my goodness, it's so
uncomfortable underfoot.


00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.200
Come on.


00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.200
There we are.


00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.100
How is her bosom?


00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.400
I have not looked at the archduchess's
bosom, Your Majesty.


00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.000
Oh, didn't you?
It's the first thing I look at.


00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.600
The Duc de Choiseul.


00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.500
The foreign minister
who was instrumental in this union.


00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:38.600
I shall never forget that you were
responsible for my happiness.


00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.800
And that of France.


00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.500
Please.


00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.900
Here comes the Austrian.


00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:02.000
I hope you like apple strudel.


00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:12.800
May I present Madame la Dauphine,
Marie Antoinette.


00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.600
My dear grandfather king.


00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:20.600
Welcome, madame.


00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:37.600
Let me present my grandson,
Louis Auguste.


00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:50.900
Welcome, madame.


00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:13.300
She looks like a child.


00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.000
Hello.


00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:27.500
Thank you.


00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.500
- Thank you.
- You're welcome, madame.


00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.200
Thanks.


00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.600
Hello.


00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.200
Amen.


00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:00.900
To the dauphin
and dauphine of France.


00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.800
May you have many
healthy children...


00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:07.100
...and produce an heir to our throne.


00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:25.800
Good luck.


00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:28.600
And good work.


00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:43.600
Apparently, nothing happened,
Your Majesty.


00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.400
Nothing?


00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:50.600
- Nothing.
- Nothing.


00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.500
Oh, dear.


00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:08.100
Madame...


00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:10.300
...at the morning
dressing ceremony...


00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:13.600
...rights of entry are given
to members of the high court.


00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:17.700
Major rights to princesses of the blood
and mistresses of the household...


00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:23.000
...while minor rights
to the valets and charges.


00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:35.100
Anyone with rights of entry
may enter at any time...


00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:41.500
...so you must pay attention to
acknowledging properly each arrival.


00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:44.900
And you must not
reach for anything...


00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:48.300
...for the handing of an item
to the dauphine is a guarded privilege.


00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:50.200
Must go to the highest rank
in the room.


00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:52.200
For example,
the Princesse de Lamballe...


00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.200
...is a princess of the blood
by marriage.


00:22:57.600 --> 00:22:59.200
Madame.


00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:11.900
Thank you.


00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:16.800
- It's cold.
- Yes.


00:23:17.800 --> 00:23:19.200
Good morning.


00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:24.400
So now the position must go
to the Duchess of Char...


00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:27.700
...because she is also
a princess of the blood.


00:23:39.700 --> 00:23:41.400
Hello.


00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:45.300
So now, as a member
of the royal family...


00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:49.000
...your sister-in-law, the Comtesse de
Provence, must have the honor.


00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.300
This is ridiculous.


00:24:16.400 --> 00:24:20.600
This, madame, is Versailles.


00:25:49.400 --> 00:25:52.400
So I've heard you make keys
as a hobby?


00:25:52.500 --> 00:25:53.900
Yes.


00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:01.300
And you enjoy making keys?


00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:03.900
Obviously.


00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:44.500
She had to let her servants go.
My maid knows the cook.


00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:49.400
You know everyone.


00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:53.100
Comtesse de Noailles
looks very out of sorts.


00:26:53.200 --> 00:26:56.100
I think her husband's been
causing a little problem lately...


00:26:56.200 --> 00:26:59.800
...spending far too much time
with his stable boys.


00:27:00.300 --> 00:27:01.900
Too much.


00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:05.400
Marie Antoinette looks
very pretty tonight.


00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:08.000
Yes.


00:27:08.100 --> 00:27:12.200
Darling, a new life, unfortunately.


00:27:12.600 --> 00:27:16.800
When you think about it,
this poor Marie Antoinette.


00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:19.200
So young, so...


00:27:19.300 --> 00:27:21.800
I think she should
go back to her country.


00:27:24.600 --> 00:27:26.000
Look at her, so disgusting.


00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:29.300
The comtesse is looking rather
dour this evening, don't you think?


00:27:29.300 --> 00:27:31.500
Always dour. Always tragic.


00:27:31.600 --> 00:27:34.200
Can't believe they've brought
those ghastly aunts out again.


00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:36.400
Where have they been
hiding them all these years?


00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:41.200
Oh, really? This is shocking.


00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:44.700
What is she...?


00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:48.000
It's so awful, I can't--
Oh, my goodness.


00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.200
Who is she?


00:27:53.500 --> 00:27:58.700
That lady is here
to give pleasure to the king.


00:28:01.700 --> 00:28:05.000
That's du Barry, the king's mistress.


00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:06.900
She wouldn't be allowed at court...


00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:09.800
...but the king did some maneuvering
to secure her a title.


00:28:09.900 --> 00:28:13.000
The one thing I've learned
about girls from the gutter...


00:28:13.100 --> 00:28:14.600
...is they know their jewels.


00:28:14.700 --> 00:28:17.200
No way are those fake.


00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.600
You see that?


00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:22.600
Is this the way
people are treating me?


00:28:23.400 --> 00:28:24.900
To the stocks.


00:28:25.100 --> 00:28:27.200
Nobody treats me like a lady here.


00:28:27.300 --> 00:28:30.000
Now she's staring at me.
It's so awful.


00:28:30.600 --> 00:28:33.400
- She should not be sitting at this table.
- I'll have one of--


00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:38.800
Did you hear that?


00:28:39.400 --> 00:28:42.800
- She just burped.
- Out of the whorehouse, darling.


00:28:42.800 --> 00:28:46.600
- I don't know who you're referring to.
- Everyone at this table is for sale.


00:28:46.700 --> 00:28:48.100
- Curls.
- What a little tart.


00:28:48.200 --> 00:28:51.400
Well, she's not the only one at this
table, darling. Take a look around.


00:28:51.400 --> 00:28:54.600
Look at this beautiful
Marie Antoinette. I look like her?


00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:56.900
- Don't you think so?
- A long time ago.


00:28:57.000 --> 00:29:00.800
Oh, you exaggerate.
She has blue eyes like me.


00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:03.200
I suppose she's rather sweet.
For an Austrian.


00:29:03.300 --> 00:29:06.000
I think she's delightful.
She looks like a piece of cake.


00:29:06.100 --> 00:29:08.800
Be interesting to see
how long she lasts.


00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:22.200
Good afternoon, Your Majesty.


00:29:24.400 --> 00:29:26.200
How is your grandson, the dauphin?


00:29:26.400 --> 00:29:29.000
He's off hunting the stag.


00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:34.100
<i>She doesn't seem</i>
<i>the least bit interested in him.</i>


00:29:34.100 --> 00:29:37.400
<i>She is Austrian. They're not exactly</i>
<i>the warmest people.</i>


00:29:37.500 --> 00:29:40.700
<i>But it's true. Her brother Joseph</i>
<i>is so cold. He's an awful man.</i>


00:29:40.800 --> 00:29:44.700
<i>They say in Austria,</i>
<i>that she was with child...</i>


00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:53.200
What a hunt today.


00:29:58.100 --> 00:30:00.100
I'm exhausted.


00:30:52.400 --> 00:30:54.300
Would you like some meat?


00:31:00.700 --> 00:31:02.500
<i>Your Royal Highness...</i>


00:31:02.700 --> 00:31:06.400
...handing out cold meats
to a hunting party...


00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:09.300
...is not the most becoming conduct
for a future queen of France.


00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:12.500
I was just trying to be a nice wife
for the dauphin's hunt.


00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:13.800
Surely there's no harm in that.


00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:17.700
And I received a letter from
your mother warning you not to ride...


00:31:17.700 --> 00:31:20.100
...as this is one of
the leading causes of miscarriages.


00:31:20.200 --> 00:31:24.200
Well, as everyone knows,
there's no danger of that.


00:31:25.100 --> 00:31:26.300
And it's not my fault.


00:31:26.500 --> 00:31:30.400
Do you realize the consequences of
an unconsummated royal marriage?


00:31:30.400 --> 00:31:32.400
That it could be annulled?


00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:35.700
Your mother has asked that
you take this matter very seriously.


00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:39.300
And do everything
in your power...


00:31:40.600 --> 00:31:42.500
...to inspire the dauphin.


00:31:43.800 --> 00:31:46.000
I'll do what I can.


00:31:46.100 --> 00:31:49.200
Of course I want to please
the dauphin and my mother.


00:31:49.400 --> 00:31:52.600
You'll have no influence over the king
and dauphin without a pregnancy.


00:31:52.600 --> 00:31:55.400
Madame, you have
the alliance to consider.


00:31:55.500 --> 00:31:58.800
Letting everyone down
would be my greatest unhappiness.


00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:03.300
I am pleased madame
is taking this seriously.


00:32:06.600 --> 00:32:08.100
Oh, is Mops on his way?


00:32:08.900 --> 00:32:11.200
I'm working on it...


00:32:11.300 --> 00:32:16.000
...but Your Royal Highness has
more pressing matters to attend to.


00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:22.100
Oh, and I received this letter
from your mother.


00:32:31.500 --> 00:32:32.900
<i>Dearest Antoinette:</i>


00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:37.100
<i>It is clear that the heart</i>
<i>of your problems in your new home...</i>


00:32:37.100 --> 00:32:42.900
<i>...is your inability to inspire</i>
<i>sexual passion in your husband.</i>


00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:47.600
<i>There is no reason a girl</i>
<i>with so many charms as you...</i>


00:32:47.600 --> 00:32:50.400
<i>...should be in this situation.</i>


00:32:50.500 --> 00:32:54.200
<i>Remember, you represent</i>
<i>the future...</i>


00:32:54.200 --> 00:32:57.600
<i>...and nothing is certain</i>
<i>about your place there...</i>


00:32:57.700 --> 00:33:03.000
<i>...until the final physical act to crown</i>
<i>the Franco-Austrian alliance...</i>


00:33:02.900 --> 00:33:05.100
<i>...is performed.</i>


00:33:40.100 --> 00:33:42.000
It's cold.


00:33:42.100 --> 00:33:44.200
It is a bit chilly.
Shall I get you a blanket?


00:33:44.300 --> 00:33:47.200
No. It's okay.


00:33:53.700 --> 00:33:57.000
Are those your feet?
They're like icicles.


00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:04.500
Well...


00:34:07.600 --> 00:34:09.300
...sleep well.


00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:14.000
Thank you.


00:34:17.300 --> 00:34:19.800
- Night.
- Good night.


00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:04.800
Your hair always looks so pretty.


00:35:04.900 --> 00:35:06.900
- Oh, do you think so?
- Yeah, it's gorgeous.


00:35:07.100 --> 00:35:09.700
- It's not what I'm used to. It is.
- It's so nice to be blond.


00:35:09.700 --> 00:35:11.500
- Have you been to see Léonard?
- No.


00:35:11.700 --> 00:35:13.600
My head is in agony.


00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:16.700
- This morning, I think, you know--
- Did he pull it?


00:35:16.700 --> 00:35:18.400
Léonard must've been
in a bad mood...


00:35:18.600 --> 00:35:21.300
...because he was pulling
my hair so hard.


00:35:21.400 --> 00:35:25.400
And I want to tell him, you know, it's
not my fault if he's had a bad morning.


00:35:25.400 --> 00:35:27.800
Don't take it out on my scalp.


00:35:34.900 --> 00:35:36.800
That was unnecessary.


00:35:37.800 --> 00:35:39.200
Watch it.


00:35:58.800 --> 00:36:00.900
I would love to go
to the opera in Paris.


00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:03.800
Why go to the opera when we can
listen to the comtesse here?


00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:06.300
Must she sing all night?


00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:11.500
Can't you do something
about your wife?


00:36:13.800 --> 00:36:17.400
Madame, shall we retire
to make love all night?


00:36:19.600 --> 00:36:21.300
Four times last night wasn't enough.


00:36:34.400 --> 00:36:36.800
Dear Antoinette:


00:36:37.900 --> 00:36:42.700
I am extremely concerned
with your situation.


00:36:44.100 --> 00:36:49.300
Fortunately, the king doesn't show
preference for your sister-in-law.


00:36:49.300 --> 00:36:54.600
But what if she becomes pregnant?


00:36:54.600 --> 00:36:57.800
<i>Also, I have heard...</i>


00:36:57.800 --> 00:37:02.000
<i>...that you are not making</i>
<i>invitations to Madame du Barry.</i>


00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:08.200
<i>Snubbing the king's favorite,</i>
<i>in your position...</i>


00:37:08.200 --> 00:37:14.100
<i>...is extremely unwise.</i>


00:37:16.600 --> 00:37:18.200
- Du Barry is dreadful.
- Dreadful.


00:37:18.400 --> 00:37:20.900
The way she dresses.
She thinks she is the queen.


00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:24.400
Yes, she does.
And those ridiculous pet monkeys.


00:37:24.400 --> 00:37:25.600
Where does she come from?


00:37:25.800 --> 00:37:28.000
From every bed in Paris.


00:37:28.100 --> 00:37:31.400
You know, we didn't think she'd
last long until she married the comte...


00:37:31.400 --> 00:37:34.000
...and then he was conveniently
shipped away somewhere.


00:37:34.100 --> 00:37:35.600
She doesn't stay in the boudoir.


00:37:35.700 --> 00:37:36.900
- She's political.
- Very.


00:37:37.100 --> 00:37:39.300
And extremely anti-Choiseul.


00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:40.900
And I don't want to say this...


00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:43.700
...but I don't think that she has
greeted you with respect.


00:37:43.800 --> 00:37:45.400
That's just my opinion.


00:37:45.600 --> 00:37:48.200
Ambassador Mercy says
I must pay her a visit.


00:37:48.300 --> 00:37:50.700
Well, if we invited you to tea
at the last minute...


00:37:50.800 --> 00:37:53.200
...you wouldn't be able to,
would you?


00:37:56.500 --> 00:37:59.900
She died giving birth
to her tenth child.


00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.200
What a pity. What a pity.


00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:04.900
- There was blood all over--
- Here comes our little Austrian.


00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:07.200
- Good afternoon, madame.
- Good afternoon.


00:38:07.300 --> 00:38:08.800
Good afternoon. You look lovely.


00:38:08.900 --> 00:38:10.700
Oh, thank you. So do you.


00:38:10.800 --> 00:38:12.100
Thank you.


00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:14.900
Look at du Barry.
What is she wearing now?


00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:17.300
Another one of her exotic fantasies?


00:38:17.400 --> 00:38:20.200
She can't pass a mirror
without seducing it.


00:38:20.200 --> 00:38:22.600
Do you think she's wearing
enough jewelry?


00:38:23.600 --> 00:38:25.000
Never enough for du Barry.


00:38:25.100 --> 00:38:27.100
She's coming.


00:38:29.200 --> 00:38:30.900
Oh, I love your shoes, Victoire.


00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:33.400
Oh, why, thank you.
I got them from Christian in Paris.


00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:36.600
- Oh, I must call on him.
- Yes, you must. He's wonderful.


00:39:25.700 --> 00:39:30.400
Madame du Barry would like
to offer you some diamonds.


00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:33.500
I have enough diamonds.


00:39:33.600 --> 00:39:37.600
Snubbing the king's favorite is publicly
criticizing the king's behavior.


00:39:37.600 --> 00:39:39.700
All you need do is say
a few words to her.


00:39:39.800 --> 00:39:42.000
Because of rank she is not
allowed to speak first.


00:39:42.100 --> 00:39:43.900
I certainly have nothing
to say to her.


00:39:44.100 --> 00:39:46.400
Why should I approve of his
cavorting with a harlot?


00:39:46.500 --> 00:39:49.100
- Your Royal Highness.
- Well, that's what she is.


00:39:49.200 --> 00:39:52.400
Everyone knows she's from a brothel
and that title was bought for her.


00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:55.400
Your mother and I
are very concerned.


00:39:55.500 --> 00:39:58.900
Du Barry has been complaining to
the king that you will not address her.


00:39:58.900 --> 00:40:01.400
And you cannot afford
to fall out of favor with the king.


00:40:01.500 --> 00:40:03.600
Especially as your marriage...


00:40:04.200 --> 00:40:06.500
...not exactly on solid ground.


00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:10.200
Fine. I'll talk to her.


00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:34.500
There are a lot of people
at Versailles today.


00:40:35.300 --> 00:40:37.100
Yes, there are.


00:41:05.100 --> 00:41:08.400
Those are my last words
to that woman.


00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:28.000
The first mechanical locks
were made of wood.


00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:38.300
Records show them in use
some 4000 years ago in Egypt.


00:42:17.900 --> 00:42:20.700
Any good fans? That one's pretty.


00:42:20.800 --> 00:42:22.500
- Evening or daytime?
- I like lace.


00:42:24.100 --> 00:42:26.600
These are so du Barry.


00:42:26.800 --> 00:42:30.500
- Do you like these for hair?
- It's beautiful.


00:42:30.600 --> 00:42:32.600
- You don't think it's too much?
- Maybe one.


00:42:32.700 --> 00:42:34.800
- One feather?
- Yeah.


00:42:34.900 --> 00:42:36.100
Or in white?


00:42:36.200 --> 00:42:38.600
Can we get these in white, maybe?


00:42:38.700 --> 00:42:40.200
I don't know if I like that one.


00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:43.100
I love these.


00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:44.900
Do you want these too?


00:42:45.100 --> 00:42:46.400
Yeah, but in pink.


00:42:46.500 --> 00:42:49.400
Oh, okay. Two in pink.


00:42:49.500 --> 00:42:52.300
Has madame read the brief
on our current situation?


00:42:52.400 --> 00:42:54.600
No, I haven't read it yet.


00:42:54.700 --> 00:42:57.100
Can you just tell me about it?


00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:03.400
Well, the reforms in Poland by King
Poniatowski have led to civil war.


00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:06.800
The Russians and the Austrians
have taken over a third of Poland...


00:43:06.800 --> 00:43:08.700
...which is, of course, distressing...


00:43:08.900 --> 00:43:11.900
...as Poland is a friend and ally
of France.


00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:17.600
Which sleeve do you like?
With ruffles or without?


00:43:18.600 --> 00:43:20.600
Have you been paying
any attention?


00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:24.600
Your mother is relying on you
to smooth over this crisis.


00:43:24.700 --> 00:43:27.500
Where will I be if there's a rupture
between our two families?


00:43:28.800 --> 00:43:31.800
Am I to be Austrian
or the dauphine of France?


00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:35.400
You must be both.


00:43:39.800 --> 00:43:43.000
- <i>Well, I heard that she bought a boy.</i>
- <i>No.</i>


00:43:43.100 --> 00:43:46.600
<i>Yes, I heard. She found a peasant</i>
<i>boy by the side of the street...</i>


00:43:46.600 --> 00:43:48.700
<i>...and took him in like a stray dog.</i>


00:43:48.800 --> 00:43:51.400
Well, it's not as if
she can have one of her own.


00:43:51.500 --> 00:43:53.500
Maybe if she spent
less time with Lamballe...


00:43:53.600 --> 00:43:55.700
...and more time with her husband...


00:43:55.900 --> 00:43:58.000
...there wouldn't be a problem.


00:43:58.100 --> 00:44:00.900
Well, let's not forget
she is an Austrian spy.


00:44:00.900 --> 00:44:04.200
And I can't imagine
that's very warm in the bedroom.


00:44:05.700 --> 00:44:08.700
Come, my little truffle cake.


00:44:09.200 --> 00:44:11.300
I'm going to ravage you.


00:44:11.700 --> 00:44:14.500
- Will you come back right away?
- Yes, my sweet.


00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:17.300
Just a quick hunting excursion,
we'll be back straightaway.


00:44:17.300 --> 00:44:22.200
I will be humiliated
before the court and the public...


00:44:22.200 --> 00:44:25.100
...if your brother's new wife
becomes pregnant before I do.


00:44:25.200 --> 00:44:28.800
When I return from Saint-Cloud,
you can be sure...


00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:30.800
...that I will resume my regime.


00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:35.200
And hopefully everything
will go swimmingly.


00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:16.000
I have absolutely no intention of
breaking the alliance with Austria.


00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:18.500
I am very relieved to hear that,
Your Majesty.


00:45:18.600 --> 00:45:21.200
But what on earth is going on
with that young couple?


00:45:21.300 --> 00:45:23.100
It's a disaster.


00:45:23.800 --> 00:45:27.400
Send for Dr. Lassonne to visit them.


00:45:27.500 --> 00:45:29.400
Yes, of course.


00:45:31.700 --> 00:45:34.900
Do you find your body responsive?


00:45:34.900 --> 00:45:36.300
What?


00:45:36.900 --> 00:45:40.200
Do you find your body responsive?


00:45:47.400 --> 00:45:50.400
What do you eat for breakfast?


00:45:50.500 --> 00:45:52.000
Hot chocolate.


00:45:52.100 --> 00:45:54.200
Hot chocolate.


00:46:26.400 --> 00:46:28.300
Hello?


00:46:28.600 --> 00:46:31.000
Hello, Yolande.


00:46:33.800 --> 00:46:35.300
How lovely to see you.


00:46:35.500 --> 00:46:38.800
Yes. This is
the Duchesse de Polignac.


00:46:38.800 --> 00:46:40.400
- Hello.
- Your Majesty.


00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:42.400
- We haven't seen you for a while.
- I know.


00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:46.200
I've been in St. Petersburg,
where I met Dimitri.


00:46:47.600 --> 00:46:51.500
Isn't he divine?
Have you ever been with a Russian?


00:46:51.700 --> 00:46:53.600
- No, I--
- They're so bossy.


00:46:53.700 --> 00:46:58.200
Look how fat the marquis's gotten.
Hope he doesn't break the chair.


00:46:58.200 --> 00:47:01.300
Is he still sleeping with Camille?


00:47:01.400 --> 00:47:04.300
Anyway, I must be off.
It was lovely to meet you.


00:47:42.500 --> 00:47:43.800
Quiet.


00:47:43.900 --> 00:47:46.600
Applause is not usually permitted
at court performances.


00:47:46.700 --> 00:47:49.900
Why not? It was wonderful.


00:47:50.700 --> 00:47:52.100
Clap, clap.


00:47:52.200 --> 00:47:54.000
Clap.


00:49:11.600 --> 00:49:13.700
<i>Dearest Antoinette:</i>


00:49:13.800 --> 00:49:18.500
<i>I'm pleased to tell you how wonderful</i>
<i>your brothers and sisters are doing...</i>


00:49:18.500 --> 00:49:20.200
<i>...in their marriages.</i>


00:49:20.300 --> 00:49:23.100
<i>Maria Carolina is pregnant...</i>


00:49:23.300 --> 00:49:26.200
<i>...expecting her first child in June.</i>


00:49:26.300 --> 00:49:29.200
<i>And Ferdinand is enchanted</i>
<i>with Beatrice...</i>


00:49:29.300 --> 00:49:32.400
<i>...having made her his wife at once.</i>


00:49:32.400 --> 00:49:36.700
<i>All this news, which should fill me</i>
<i>with contentment...</i>


00:49:36.700 --> 00:49:42.100
<i>...is diminished by reflections</i>
<i>on your dangerous situation.</i>


00:49:42.100 --> 00:49:44.400
<i>Everything depends on the wife...</i>


00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:47.600
<i>...if she is willing and sweet.</i>


00:49:47.700 --> 00:49:49.500
<i>I can't repeat enough...</i>


00:49:49.600 --> 00:49:54.600
<i>...the importance for you</i>
<i>to employ charm and patience...</i>


00:49:54.600 --> 00:50:00.000
<i>...never ill humor, to remedy</i>
<i>this unfortunate situation.</i>


00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:03.100
<i>Remember, nothing is certain</i>
<i>about your place there...</i>


00:50:03.100 --> 00:50:06.400
<i>...until an heir is produced.</i>


00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:31.000
- Excuse me.
- It's all right.


00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:55.500
I'm sorry.


00:50:55.700 --> 00:50:57.300
That's all right.


00:50:57.400 --> 00:51:00.400
- I'm sorry.
- It's all right.


00:51:03.900 --> 00:51:06.700
- Good night.
- Good night.


00:51:33.500 --> 00:51:38.400
Your Majesties are requested at the
delivery of Comtesse de Provence.


00:51:47.800 --> 00:51:50.600
Bravo, bravo.


00:51:51.100 --> 00:51:54.200
- Oh, wonderful!
- It's a healthy baby boy.


00:51:54.300 --> 00:51:57.600
Oh, my God. How happy I am.


00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.200
Let me see my nephew.
The new Duc d'Angoulême.


00:52:04.800 --> 00:52:06.600
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.


00:52:06.800 --> 00:52:09.900
It's the first Bourbon prince
of his generation.


00:52:10.200 --> 00:52:12.400
He's so beautiful.


00:52:14.200 --> 00:52:16.600
It's barren. What do you expect?


00:52:17.500 --> 00:52:20.000
When will you give us an heir?


00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:22.900
I hear she's frigid.


00:53:44.700 --> 00:53:47.200
I like the pink. It's like candy.


00:53:57.500 --> 00:54:00.200
This is wonderful.


00:54:01.100 --> 00:54:02.800
I love this.


00:54:03.600 --> 00:54:05.100
Oh, it's a classic.


00:54:16.100 --> 00:54:18.300
Could we get
some more champagne?


00:55:09.800 --> 00:55:11.500
Monsieur Léonard.


00:55:26.200 --> 00:55:27.500
Ravishing.


00:55:30.600 --> 00:55:32.400
Oh, Léonard.


00:55:32.700 --> 00:55:34.300
You're the best.


00:55:34.700 --> 00:55:37.700
- It's not too much, is it?
- No.


00:56:02.200 --> 00:56:04.900
We should all go to Paris
for the masked ball.


00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:08.000
We're not allowed to go
without a formal reception.


00:56:08.700 --> 00:56:10.800
Well, if it's a masked ball...


00:56:10.900 --> 00:56:13.600
...no one would have to know,
would they?


00:56:23.600 --> 00:56:24.800
Sorry.


00:56:50.500 --> 00:56:51.900
Which way?


00:56:54.800 --> 00:56:56.000
Come on.


00:57:30.600 --> 00:57:32.000
Excuse me.


00:57:32.400 --> 00:57:33.700
Excuse me.


00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.500
Where do you come from, monsieur?


00:58:02.900 --> 00:58:04.200
Versailles.


00:58:06.300 --> 00:58:11.100
And has the dauphin
done the deed yet?


00:58:12.100 --> 00:58:13.300
What?


00:58:13.500 --> 00:58:16.400
Has the dauphin deflowered
the dauphine?


00:58:16.500 --> 00:58:20.600
- Excuse me?
- I'd love to do the honors, you know.


00:58:46.800 --> 00:58:49.400
Doesn't interest me. Cheers.


00:59:03.300 --> 00:59:05.400
Look at that sword.


00:59:05.500 --> 00:59:08.200
I'd like to see what he could
do with that.


00:59:09.600 --> 00:59:11.700
Oh, who's he talking to?


00:59:11.800 --> 00:59:14.100
Hideous dress she's wearing.


00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:24.800
Pretend you're having
a really good time.


00:59:26.500 --> 00:59:27.900
Have fun.


00:59:30.300 --> 00:59:34.500
- Do I know you?
- No. I don't think so.


00:59:36.200 --> 00:59:39.200
Are you making
any progress with her?


00:59:40.300 --> 00:59:41.600
Possibly.


00:59:43.300 --> 00:59:44.900
Are you going to tell me
who you are?


00:59:48.100 --> 00:59:49.700
Are you?


00:59:50.000 --> 00:59:52.400
Count Fersen of the Swedish army.


00:59:53.900 --> 00:59:55.200
Count Fersen.


01:00:02.300 --> 01:00:04.300
That's the dauphine.


01:00:22.600 --> 01:00:24.700
We must go.
It's half past three in the morning.


01:00:24.800 --> 01:00:26.500
No. Let's just stay a little longer.


01:00:26.600 --> 01:00:29.000
- Oh, please. Let's go. Come on.
- Please, please.


01:00:29.100 --> 01:00:30.300
Finally.


01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:36.200
Do you know of Count Fersen?


01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:39.800
Yes! Count Fersen, of course.


01:00:39.900 --> 01:00:41.900
Beatrice de la Falaise
was with him last summer.


01:00:42.100 --> 01:00:43.700
He's got quite a reputation,
you know.


01:00:43.900 --> 01:00:46.500
Comtesse de Sevigny.
She was with him too.


01:02:27.900 --> 01:02:29.600
Good morning.


01:02:30.900 --> 01:02:33.500
- What is it?
- The king has fallen ill.


01:02:33.600 --> 01:02:34.900
Is it serious?


01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:36.300
Smallpox.


01:02:38.200 --> 01:02:40.400
He doesn't have long.


01:02:40.500 --> 01:02:45.900
You know, we cannot take his
confession while he has a mistress.


01:02:49.500 --> 01:02:51.900
It will be taken care of.


01:02:52.500 --> 01:02:54.500
Madame du Barry...


01:02:55.500 --> 01:02:59.000
...I'm sick and know
what I have to do.


01:03:00.400 --> 01:03:02.500
<i>Rest assured...</i>


01:03:02.700 --> 01:03:05.000
<i>...I shall always...</i>


01:03:05.100 --> 01:03:09.000
<i>...have the most tender feelings</i>
<i>of friendship for you.</i>


01:03:38.200 --> 01:03:40.100
Bring me du Barry.


01:03:41.800 --> 01:03:44.300
She is gone, Your Majesty.


01:03:59.400 --> 01:04:03.100
The king is dead.
Long live Louis XVI.


01:04:09.400 --> 01:04:13.000
Your Majesties,
I am at your loyal service.


01:04:23.100 --> 01:04:28.100
Dear God, guide us and protect us.
We are too young to reign.


01:04:33.500 --> 01:04:38.000
May God crown you
with a crown of glory.


01:05:26.500 --> 01:05:28.400
How marvelous.


01:05:29.200 --> 01:05:31.500
Here are two for me and the queen.


01:05:31.700 --> 01:05:33.400
Happy birthday, darling!


01:05:39.800 --> 01:05:42.300
One, two, three.


01:05:42.400 --> 01:05:45.300
Happy birthday!


01:05:54.500 --> 01:05:58.100
Happy birthday, darling.
Eighteen. Happy birthday.


01:06:03.900 --> 01:06:05.100
Big stakes! Come on now!


01:06:06.500 --> 01:06:08.100
That one.


01:06:08.500 --> 01:06:09.700
That one's for me.


01:06:11.300 --> 01:06:12.900
What's coming?


01:06:18.300 --> 01:06:19.600
Amazing.


01:06:30.100 --> 01:06:31.500
Here are two.


01:06:33.300 --> 01:06:35.200
So pretty!


01:06:45.700 --> 01:06:47.600
Oh, Léonard.


01:06:47.900 --> 01:06:49.100
Thank you.


01:06:52.200 --> 01:06:54.100
Okay, come round to the salon.


01:06:54.200 --> 01:06:55.900
Speak to le beau Julian.


01:06:56.200 --> 01:06:59.200
- First. And then you'll see me.
- Marvelous!


01:06:59.300 --> 01:07:01.000
I've heard he likes men as well.


01:07:01.100 --> 01:07:03.200
No. No. It's not true.


01:07:03.900 --> 01:07:05.600
Do you want some cherry?


01:07:08.200 --> 01:07:10.900
I love your hair.
What's going on there?


01:07:11.000 --> 01:07:12.500
Everything.


01:07:12.800 --> 01:07:15.300
- It's fantastic.
- It's full of secrets.


01:07:24.500 --> 01:07:26.200
You're winning, I hope.


01:07:28.900 --> 01:07:30.100
Madame, it's quite late.


01:07:30.300 --> 01:07:32.600
I think it's time for
the dealers to return to Paris.


01:07:32.700 --> 01:07:35.700
You said we could play
but you never specified for how long.


01:07:35.700 --> 01:07:38.400
- You're worthless.
- I won again!


01:07:39.300 --> 01:07:41.900
- Give me my chips.
- How'd you get so good at this?


01:07:42.100 --> 01:07:43.800
- Good night.
- Oh, no. Don't go to sleep.


01:07:43.900 --> 01:07:47.000
We're gonna watch the sunrise.
Don't you want to see that?


01:07:47.000 --> 01:07:49.000
I'd rather get
some much-needed sleep.


01:07:49.200 --> 01:07:51.500
Have you ever watched the sunrise?


01:07:51.800 --> 01:07:53.700
When I rise early for the hunt,
my dear.


01:07:53.900 --> 01:07:55.600
- That doesn't count.
- It's your turn.


01:07:55.700 --> 01:07:58.300
Try not to lose our whole fortune.


01:07:59.100 --> 01:08:00.700
On a roll.


01:08:04.900 --> 01:08:06.100
I'm taking off.


01:08:06.200 --> 01:08:08.800
That's impressive.
That is very impressive.


01:08:13.200 --> 01:08:14.700
Wait! Wait! Wait!


01:08:14.900 --> 01:08:16.400
Spin with me!


01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:18.300
Wait!


01:08:21.500 --> 01:08:22.900
Come along.


01:08:31.300 --> 01:08:34.400
Come on. Come on, people.
Move, move, move.


01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:54.800
Isn't that the most beautiful thing
you've ever seen?


01:08:59.600 --> 01:09:02.000
- Happy birthday.
- Happy birthday.


01:09:02.100 --> 01:09:04.300
- Cheers. For the birthday girl.
- Happy birthday.


01:09:04.800 --> 01:09:06.300
To the new day.


01:09:07.400 --> 01:09:08.800
And the next one.


01:09:09.200 --> 01:09:11.500
I think I have a fly
in my champagne.


01:10:49.200 --> 01:10:52.900
I would like to plant oaks
all along these paths.


01:10:52.900 --> 01:10:54.600
How long will that take?


01:10:54.700 --> 01:11:00.000
It will take two weeks to get them,
but they will be quite small.


01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:04.100
What if I want them that size?


01:11:04.800 --> 01:11:06.900
It will take at least three years.


01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:08.300
- Three years?
- Yes.


01:11:08.400 --> 01:11:10.300
Well, can't they bring in
bigger ones?


01:11:10.400 --> 01:11:12.200
Well, I can see.


01:11:16.600 --> 01:11:21.000
Your Majesty, you have spent
over 50,000 already this month.


01:11:21.500 --> 01:11:24.000
There is nothing left
to go to your charities.


01:11:24.300 --> 01:11:26.800
Your Majesty? Léonard is here
to fit your new wigs.


01:11:26.800 --> 01:11:29.800
All right.
I'll get the small trees.


01:11:29.900 --> 01:11:32.800
And I'll ask Louis for the money
for the Young Mothers' Fund.


01:11:39.400 --> 01:11:43.700
The Americans are asking for help
in their revolution.


01:11:44.800 --> 01:11:47.500
Well, I can't exactly see
assisting those...


01:11:47.600 --> 01:11:49.900
...who are rejecting their sovereign.


01:11:50.100 --> 01:11:53.300
But it would make
a strong statement to England.


01:11:53.800 --> 01:11:55.600
Can our finances take the strain?


01:11:55.800 --> 01:11:58.200
Oh, taxes will be raised slightly.


01:11:58.300 --> 01:12:01.200
I recommend we help
our American brothers...


01:12:01.300 --> 01:12:04.400
...and show the rest of Europe
our strength.


01:12:06.600 --> 01:12:10.800
All right, then.
Send funds to America.


01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:33.600
Madame, your brother, the emperor,
is in the salon waiting for you.


01:12:33.700 --> 01:12:35.900
He's here? Thank you.


01:12:45.700 --> 01:12:47.400
Have you come to take me home?


01:12:47.900 --> 01:12:50.800
Unfortunately, I can't kidnap
the queen of France.


01:12:50.800 --> 01:12:53.400
Is your hair quite tall enough today?


01:12:53.400 --> 01:12:56.900
Maybe you can keep a pet
in there or something.


01:12:59.400 --> 01:13:02.100
The emperor of China
sent me this tea.


01:13:03.600 --> 01:13:05.600
Watch the flower.


01:13:09.300 --> 01:13:11.400
Isn't it divine?


01:13:11.900 --> 01:13:13.300
Yes.


01:13:16.200 --> 01:13:17.700
It's jasmine.


01:13:31.100 --> 01:13:35.900
As your brother, I have to lecture you
about your constant gambling...


01:13:35.900 --> 01:13:39.700
...and choice of friends,
like the Duchesse de Polignac.


01:13:39.800 --> 01:13:42.600
Do you think she's the proper
lady-in-waiting for a queen?


01:13:42.600 --> 01:13:45.300
But she's fun. She makes me laugh.


01:13:45.400 --> 01:13:46.800
And your constant parties.


01:13:47.000 --> 01:13:49.500
I mean, they can hardly leave you
enough time to spend...


01:13:49.600 --> 01:13:51.900
...alone with your husband.


01:13:52.000 --> 01:13:54.000
I'm sure our mother has worried you.


01:13:54.600 --> 01:13:57.600
Yes. Well, of course she has.


01:14:01.000 --> 01:14:03.900
I think I'm gonna talk to young Louis.


01:14:19.000 --> 01:14:20.400
Magnificent.


01:14:25.800 --> 01:14:29.100
We have a female elephant
in our Austrian menagerie.


01:14:29.700 --> 01:14:32.400
Well, perhaps we could arrange
a marriage.


01:14:36.500 --> 01:14:38.200
So...


01:14:38.400 --> 01:14:42.000
...I thought we could have a little talk
about the marriage bed.


01:14:44.100 --> 01:14:46.200
The doctor said I was fit.


01:14:46.300 --> 01:14:47.900
Good.


01:14:48.000 --> 01:14:50.100
What goes on exactly?


01:14:57.100 --> 01:15:00.500
I understand you have
a certain passion for locks.


01:15:00.500 --> 01:15:01.900
Yes.


01:15:01.900 --> 01:15:05.100
Well, sometimes when
a key doesn't quite fit...


01:15:05.200 --> 01:15:08.400
<i>The problem is only that</i>
<i>the king and queen of France...</i>


01:15:08.500 --> 01:15:10.600
<i>...are complete blunderers.</i>


01:15:10.700 --> 01:15:14.000
<i>There's nothing really wrong</i>
<i>with Louis XVI.</i>


01:15:14.000 --> 01:15:18.100
<i>Everything works,</i>
<i>just not at the right time.</i>


01:15:18.100 --> 01:15:23.300
<i>I think after our conversation,</i>
<i>the great work will be accomplished.</i>


01:16:06.400 --> 01:16:08.000
Very warm in here.


01:16:08.400 --> 01:16:10.500
I can't even believe she's getting
enough air.


01:16:26.000 --> 01:16:27.900
Is it a boy?


01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:31.300
It's a girl, look.


01:16:31.400 --> 01:16:33.900
She's unconscious.
We must get her air.


01:16:34.100 --> 01:16:35.800
Please, the queen needs air.


01:16:35.900 --> 01:16:39.100
Excuse me. Excuse me. Excuse me.


01:16:39.200 --> 01:16:41.800
Get back. Back.
Get back, please.


01:16:41.900 --> 01:16:43.600
Everybody, please.


01:16:43.900 --> 01:16:45.300
Get back.


01:16:57.200 --> 01:16:58.300
Oh, he's beautiful.


01:17:01.800 --> 01:17:03.900
You are adorable.


01:17:04.500 --> 01:17:06.200
It's a girl.


01:17:10.500 --> 01:17:12.700
Poor little girl.


01:17:12.800 --> 01:17:18.100
You are not what was desired,
but you are no less dear to me.


01:17:19.700 --> 01:17:22.400
A boy would be the son of France...


01:17:22.500 --> 01:17:26.400
...but you, Marie Thérèse,
shall be mine.


01:17:28.000 --> 01:17:29.400
Come look.


01:17:30.700 --> 01:17:33.000
Oh, she's so small.


01:17:33.900 --> 01:17:35.300
Look at her hands.


01:17:46.700 --> 01:17:48.400
I would like to feed her myself.


01:17:48.600 --> 01:17:50.900
But, madame,
we have the nurse for that.


01:17:51.500 --> 01:17:54.800
And you know, it's not a good idea
in your fragile condition.


01:17:57.100 --> 01:17:58.600
Madame.


01:18:05.700 --> 01:18:09.500
May I present you with
your new retreat, the Petit Trianon.


01:18:11.800 --> 01:18:13.000
Thank you.


01:19:27.300 --> 01:19:31.900
I want something
more simple. Natural.


01:19:32.400 --> 01:19:34.100
<i>To wear in the garden.</i>


01:19:46.800 --> 01:19:50.200
Are you getting food for the little lamb?
Let's feed the lamb.


01:19:50.200 --> 01:19:51.900
Marie Thérèse, come here.


01:19:53.700 --> 01:19:56.500
You do it. You do it.
You feed the lamb.


01:19:56.500 --> 01:19:57.900
You feed the lamb.


01:20:05.600 --> 01:20:07.300
Little lamby.


01:20:26.300 --> 01:20:28.200
Beautiful.


01:20:28.800 --> 01:20:31.100
What is this? It's an egg.


01:20:32.400 --> 01:20:35.700
Welcome to my little village.
I love it here.


01:20:35.800 --> 01:20:38.100
- Really special.
- It's my heaven.


01:20:40.100 --> 01:20:41.700
- Hello.
- Sweet.


01:20:41.800 --> 01:20:45.100
Oh, look, the chickens
are out. Fabulous.


01:20:45.500 --> 01:20:47.200
Oh, the lilies look so beautiful.


01:20:47.400 --> 01:20:50.000
- It's heavenly.
- Hello.


01:20:50.000 --> 01:20:52.400
Come on, you little chickens.
Come on, little chickens!


01:20:52.500 --> 01:20:54.600
Oh, look at those little things. Hello!


01:20:54.700 --> 01:20:56.200
That one's named after me.


01:20:56.400 --> 01:21:00.300
Oh, this is my favorite, all the fresh
herbs. They smell so good.


01:21:00.400 --> 01:21:03.600
You've got to brush the dirt off a bit,
but they're quite clean after that.


01:21:04.500 --> 01:21:08.000
Oh, we must do this more often.
I love the country.


01:21:10.800 --> 01:21:12.800
Where'd you get this from?


01:21:13.800 --> 01:21:17.400
- Wait till you try this milk.
- Oh, what beautiful porcelain.


01:21:17.500 --> 01:21:20.200
- How lovely.
- That one's very good.


01:21:22.600 --> 01:21:23.900
One of these.


01:21:25.600 --> 01:21:27.200
You must try the milk.


01:21:27.400 --> 01:21:28.600
Thank you.


01:21:33.700 --> 01:21:35.200
Rousseau says:


01:21:35.300 --> 01:21:39.100
"If we assume man has been
corrupted by an artificial civilization...


01:21:39.400 --> 01:21:41.300
<i>...what is the natural state?</i>


01:21:41.900 --> 01:21:44.600
<i>The state of nature</i>
<i>from which he has been removed?</i>


01:21:46.300 --> 01:21:50.000
<i>Imagine wandering up</i>
<i>and down the forest...</i>


01:21:50.100 --> 01:21:53.800
<i>...without industry, without speech...</i>


01:21:53.800 --> 01:21:55.600
<i>...and without home."</i>


01:22:14.400 --> 01:22:17.400
Let's get a blue flower.


01:22:22.800 --> 01:22:24.200
Beautiful.


01:22:39.300 --> 01:22:43.400
<i>No, I think perceived austerity</i>
<i>must be encouraged...</i>


01:22:43.400 --> 01:22:47.700
...but I'm afraid the queen has
a somewhat artistic temperament...


01:22:47.700 --> 01:22:49.300
...which needs nourishing.


01:22:49.400 --> 01:22:50.700
May I speak to you?


01:22:50.900 --> 01:22:53.100
Yes. Excuse me, Father.


01:22:54.600 --> 01:22:57.500
We have not received any invitation
by the queen...


01:22:57.600 --> 01:23:00.200
...which is customary to our rank.


01:23:00.300 --> 01:23:04.500
I'm afraid the queen is not well
enough for formal entertaining...


01:23:04.600 --> 01:23:07.000
...but I will speak with her, madame.


01:23:07.500 --> 01:23:08.800
But--


01:23:10.200 --> 01:23:12.800
How can we be expected
to live in a place...


01:23:13.000 --> 01:23:15.900
...without any certainty
of our position?


01:23:16.200 --> 01:23:17.500
I don't understand.


01:23:17.600 --> 01:23:20.900
The Duchesse de Char
was very angry.


01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:23.400
But this is my escape
from all the protocol.


01:23:23.500 --> 01:23:26.700
Raumont, amongst others,
was complaining.


01:23:27.700 --> 01:23:32.400
Well, we'll invite them to the theater
for my first performance.


01:23:32.400 --> 01:23:35.600
- We'll need an audience.
- Splendid.


01:24:16.900 --> 01:24:18.700
Bravo!


01:24:20.100 --> 01:24:21.400
Bravo!


01:24:22.100 --> 01:24:23.600
Bravo!


01:24:25.400 --> 01:24:28.300
And in the end, I don't know
how they go out.


01:24:28.400 --> 01:24:31.300
- It's always raining there.
- Not like here. It's always raining.


01:24:31.400 --> 01:24:33.200
They are cheerful, I must admit.


01:24:34.500 --> 01:24:35.800
There's someone to see you.


01:24:36.000 --> 01:24:37.800
Oh, who?


01:24:43.600 --> 01:24:45.000
Good afternoon!


01:24:45.100 --> 01:24:48.400
You've come to pay me a visit.
How gallant you are.


01:24:48.500 --> 01:24:51.900
- Have you seen Marie Thérèse today?
- She's been married off.


01:24:52.000 --> 01:24:54.400
Can't we at least wait
until she's talking?


01:24:54.500 --> 01:24:55.700
If you insist.


01:24:55.800 --> 01:24:59.600
Come home. We're having a ball for
the soldiers who fought in America.


01:24:59.700 --> 01:25:01.200
I will.


01:25:04.700 --> 01:25:06.800
I hope there are
some handsome generals.


01:25:06.900 --> 01:25:09.600
They've been away from women
a long time, you know.


01:25:10.300 --> 01:25:12.900
May I also present Comte d'Estaing.


01:25:14.100 --> 01:25:18.500
Excellent victory on the capture
of Grenada. Excellent.


01:25:19.900 --> 01:25:21.600
Congratulations.


01:25:22.700 --> 01:25:26.800
Your Majesty, may I present
Colonel Smythe.


01:25:28.600 --> 01:25:31.300
May I also present Count Fersen.


01:25:33.600 --> 01:25:35.100
Count Fersen.


01:25:35.200 --> 01:25:37.700
Pleasure's all mine.


01:25:39.800 --> 01:25:41.600
Thank you, sir. Thank you.


01:25:41.900 --> 01:25:44.100
- What is this?
- It's a wild strawberry.


01:25:44.200 --> 01:25:45.700
Try it. It's quite exquisite.


01:25:47.700 --> 01:25:51.200
Honestly! "The Marriage of Figaro".
You'd love it.


01:25:51.300 --> 01:25:53.400
The servants take over the house.


01:25:53.500 --> 01:25:55.200
It's superb.


01:25:55.300 --> 01:25:57.900
The women were carrying
the verses around on their fans.


01:25:58.000 --> 01:26:00.500
Best thing I've seen for years.
You enjoyed it, didn't you?


01:26:00.700 --> 01:26:01.800
I think we saw it together.


01:26:01.900 --> 01:26:04.100
It was over three hours.
Far too long for me.


01:26:04.200 --> 01:26:06.500
- Cheers, everybody.
- To the queen.


01:26:06.600 --> 01:26:08.200
To our queen.


01:26:09.600 --> 01:26:11.600
Have a good evening.


01:26:11.700 --> 01:26:13.800
And to Raumont
for bringing the oysters.


01:26:13.900 --> 01:26:16.100
To Raumont for the oysters.


01:26:16.200 --> 01:26:18.200
And to Lamballe
for bringing the flowers.


01:26:18.300 --> 01:26:20.300
For the flowers, beautiful flowers.


01:26:20.400 --> 01:26:23.300
And to Fersen for coming
all the way from Sweden.


01:26:23.400 --> 01:26:24.600
- Yes.
- To Sweden.


01:26:24.700 --> 01:26:26.200
All the way from Sweden.


01:26:26.700 --> 01:26:29.600
That is a very long journey,
I must say.


01:26:29.700 --> 01:26:32.400
- How long was it?
- Took about ten days.


01:26:32.500 --> 01:26:34.500
Yes, ten days
is a very long time.


01:26:34.600 --> 01:26:37.400
Personally, I can't travel
that much myself.


01:26:38.300 --> 01:26:41.400
- Far too long.
- I must show you this trick.


01:26:41.400 --> 01:26:46.400
Everybody, lick your finger and then
rub it around the rim of the glass.


01:26:46.500 --> 01:26:48.400
Beautiful.


01:26:48.500 --> 01:26:51.100
- A horrible sound.
- Oh, come on. It's like angels.


01:26:51.800 --> 01:26:54.600
- It's like angels.
- It's very pretty.


01:26:54.600 --> 01:26:56.200
It is pretty, isn't it?


01:26:58.200 --> 01:27:00.900
It's very spiritual, really, isn't it?


01:27:02.400 --> 01:27:04.900
When was the last time
you went to Mass?


01:27:07.000 --> 01:27:09.400
- Of sorts.
- I haven't seen it.


01:27:09.500 --> 01:27:10.700
Ask another question.


01:27:10.900 --> 01:27:12.500
- I can ask another question?
- Yeah.


01:27:13.300 --> 01:27:14.800
Am I a male?


01:27:14.900 --> 01:27:16.200
- No.
- No.


01:27:17.000 --> 01:27:18.600
Partially.


01:27:19.500 --> 01:27:20.800
That's terrible.


01:27:20.900 --> 01:27:22.200
Oh, that's so mean.


01:27:22.500 --> 01:27:24.200
My turn, it's my turn.


01:27:24.400 --> 01:27:25.700
Am I a woman?


01:27:25.800 --> 01:27:27.900
Am I a soldier?


01:27:28.000 --> 01:27:30.800
- Do I write music?
- Yes.


01:27:30.900 --> 01:27:32.100
Am I a vegetable?


01:27:32.300 --> 01:27:34.500
- Yes. Good question.
- Yes.


01:27:35.200 --> 01:27:37.100
Am I...


01:27:38.600 --> 01:27:39.800
...from the ancient world?


01:27:39.900 --> 01:27:42.500
- Am I here?
- No.


01:27:42.600 --> 01:27:43.900
No, thank God.


01:27:44.000 --> 01:27:45.900
Am I...


01:27:46.000 --> 01:27:47.300
...present now?


01:27:47.500 --> 01:27:49.200
- Yes.
- Yes, always.


01:27:49.800 --> 01:27:52.100
- Am I--?
- You're very talented.


01:27:52.200 --> 01:27:54.300
- Am I Alexander the Great?
- Yes.


01:27:54.400 --> 01:27:56.000
Is it Mozart?


01:27:56.600 --> 01:27:59.300
- You saw!
- You've seen yours.


01:27:59.400 --> 01:28:01.100
That's the second time
I've won as well.


01:28:01.200 --> 01:28:03.700
- You saw that.
- There's something in the oysters.


01:28:14.000 --> 01:28:15.300
Be careful, please.


01:28:45.100 --> 01:28:47.900
But you should try to visit America.


01:28:48.500 --> 01:28:51.400
It's beautiful, very different
than France.


01:28:51.600 --> 01:28:54.100
Our queen seems rather fond
of looking at Count Fersen.


01:28:54.200 --> 01:28:57.000
Then you've not heard
of the Hasselhoff family singers?


01:28:57.200 --> 01:28:58.400
No.


01:28:58.500 --> 01:29:00.500
Well, he's easy on the eyes.


01:29:01.900 --> 01:29:04.200
But don't you think she favors him
too clearly?


01:29:05.000 --> 01:29:06.600
Just because it is not you?


01:29:06.700 --> 01:29:09.100
Don't you think it would be
unbecoming to our queen...


01:29:09.200 --> 01:29:11.600
...when he has quite a reputation?


01:29:11.700 --> 01:29:13.800
He amuses her,
and she likes to be amused.


01:29:14.900 --> 01:29:18.000
There's nothing unregal
in that, monsieur.


01:29:21.900 --> 01:29:24.400
- You must meet soldiers all the time.
- No, I don't.


01:29:24.500 --> 01:29:25.700
You don't?


01:30:34.700 --> 01:30:38.800
And then he took it out.
Just like that.


01:30:38.900 --> 01:30:41.500
I said, "What do you think
you'll do with that, monsieur?"


01:30:41.600 --> 01:30:43.900
Oh, good God, don't act all innocent.


01:30:44.100 --> 01:30:45.700
Please.


01:30:45.900 --> 01:30:48.400
I could have told him exactly
what to do with it.


01:30:48.400 --> 01:30:50.100
And what is that, darling?


01:30:50.300 --> 01:30:52.400
Put it back in his trousers
where it belonged.


01:30:52.500 --> 01:30:55.900
Lamballe, ladies and gentlemen,
is what we call a prude.


01:30:55.900 --> 01:30:57.300
Better than a whore.


01:30:59.400 --> 01:31:01.600
I wish I could go with you.


01:31:02.800 --> 01:31:04.500
I should kidnap you.


01:32:28.600 --> 01:32:32.200
Of course, you know
the one about the English letter.


01:32:34.700 --> 01:32:37.300
Don't you want to go to Paris,
see the opera?


01:32:37.400 --> 01:32:38.700
Your go.


01:32:38.800 --> 01:32:41.400
I'm more comfortable
just to stay here.


01:32:41.900 --> 01:32:43.300
We have everything we need.


01:32:43.400 --> 01:32:46.600
I should talk to the priest.
No, that's inexcusable.


01:32:46.700 --> 01:32:49.500
It is. It's dangerous for her safety.


01:32:49.600 --> 01:32:51.500
Goodness, a criminal
could come in here.


01:32:51.600 --> 01:32:53.700
- Cheat.
- Conceivably her husband.


01:32:54.400 --> 01:32:57.900
You know, I heard
she's not even really a duchess.


01:32:57.900 --> 01:32:59.200
Yeah, it's all a front.


01:32:59.300 --> 01:33:02.100
Her husband's a thief,
and he bought her title.


01:33:02.200 --> 01:33:04.300
Is that what happened? Really?


01:33:04.400 --> 01:33:05.900
That's what I heard.


01:33:07.900 --> 01:33:11.200
- How much did that cost?
- A fortune.


01:33:11.200 --> 01:33:13.100
It would cost a fortune, wouldn't it?


01:33:13.300 --> 01:33:16.200
To buy a title? Yes. At the court?


01:33:19.600 --> 01:33:20.800
She shouldn't be allowed.


01:33:20.900 --> 01:33:23.100
She should buy a new dress,
is what she should buy.


01:33:23.200 --> 01:33:25.600
She should buy a new dress,
yeah, you're right.


01:33:50.700 --> 01:33:52.500
Vaguely.


01:33:53.600 --> 01:33:56.000
- What are you laughing at?
- Nothing.


01:33:56.700 --> 01:33:58.500
May I be excused?


01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:00.700
Yes, of course, madame.


01:34:01.300 --> 01:34:04.100
I might go and ask her.
That way she'll tell us exactly.


01:34:04.200 --> 01:34:06.100
Ask her about her family.


01:34:51.500 --> 01:34:54.000
The problem of the debt
is grave, Your Majesty.


01:34:54.100 --> 01:34:55.700
The people of France are hungry.


01:34:55.900 --> 01:34:59.900
Sending troops to America is costing
more than what we estimated.


01:34:59.900 --> 01:35:02.300
But we can't let England win.


01:35:02.900 --> 01:35:05.500
We must show our strength.


01:35:08.600 --> 01:35:11.400
We will continue aid
to the Americans.


01:35:13.100 --> 01:35:18.000
<i>And when they went to the queen</i>
<i>to tell her her subjects had no bread...</i>


01:35:18.000 --> 01:35:20.500
<i>...do you know what she said?</i>


01:35:20.600 --> 01:35:23.000
Let them eat cake.


01:35:23.100 --> 01:35:26.000
That's such nonsense.
I would never say that.


01:35:26.400 --> 01:35:30.400
And here you're having
an orgy with quite a big group.


01:35:30.400 --> 01:35:31.900
I think I'm here sucking your toes.


01:35:32.000 --> 01:35:34.200
Don't they ever tire
of these ridiculous stories?


01:35:34.300 --> 01:35:39.200
They say you gave Thomas Jefferson
a special tour of your gardens.


01:35:40.300 --> 01:35:43.300
Is Jefferson admiring
the royal bush?


01:35:45.000 --> 01:35:47.600
- Oh, that's awful.
- Can't you do something?


01:35:48.300 --> 01:35:50.600
I'm not going to acknowledge it.


01:35:52.200 --> 01:35:54.000
The French can be fickle...


01:35:54.200 --> 01:35:58.300
...and Her Majesty would do well
to be more attentive.


01:35:59.000 --> 01:36:01.900
Life is getting harder
for the people of France.


01:36:01.900 --> 01:36:04.100
The bread shortage is grave.


01:36:04.200 --> 01:36:07.600
Well, there must be something the
king can do to ease their sufferings.


01:36:08.200 --> 01:36:11.300
Tell the court jeweler
to stop sending diamonds.


01:36:11.500 --> 01:36:14.100
You don't need any diamonds,
do you?


01:36:14.200 --> 01:36:17.000
- No.
- How pretty Madame Royale is.


01:36:17.100 --> 01:36:19.100
I'm pleased you find me so.


01:36:20.400 --> 01:36:22.200
Say thank you.


01:36:23.500 --> 01:36:26.000
She is certainly
a daughter of France.


01:36:26.100 --> 01:36:27.600
Oh, I know.


01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:31.400
What's the matter?


01:36:31.900 --> 01:36:33.700
Your mother has died.


01:36:33.800 --> 01:36:35.600
I'm so sorry.


01:36:49.700 --> 01:36:54.500
<i>Oh, my brother, I am devastated</i>
<i>by the news of our mother's death.</i>


01:36:55.000 --> 01:36:58.000
<i>You alone are left to me in Austria...</i>


01:36:58.000 --> 01:37:01.700
<i>...which is and will always be</i>
<i>so dear to me.</i>


01:37:01.800 --> 01:37:05.900
<i>Remember we are your friends,</i>
<i>your allies.</i>


01:37:06.000 --> 01:37:07.600
<i>I embrace you.</i>


01:37:21.800 --> 01:37:26.800
Madame, you have fulfilled
our wishes and those of France.


01:37:26.800 --> 01:37:28.300
You are the mother of a dauphin.


01:37:32.500 --> 01:37:36.400
May I present the dauphin of France.


01:37:51.300 --> 01:37:54.100
What a joy. The dauphin of France.


01:42:08.000 --> 01:42:11.100
Hello. Why don't you hit
the ball over there?


01:42:11.400 --> 01:42:13.500
Come on. You're gonna hit it.


01:42:20.200 --> 01:42:25.500
Your Majesty, the Bastille fortress
was stormed by an angry mob.


01:42:30.800 --> 01:42:33.700
In view of the hatred felt
for the Duchesse de Polignac...


01:42:33.800 --> 01:42:35.500
...thought to be
the queen's favorite...


01:42:35.800 --> 01:42:39.200
...I would recommend that
she leave for the Swiss border.


01:42:39.300 --> 01:42:43.600
I also must urge all of the princes
and princesses of the blood...


01:42:43.600 --> 01:42:45.000
...to leave at once.


01:42:45.200 --> 01:42:48.200
Yes, they must go. I will stay.


01:42:48.200 --> 01:42:51.600
Certainly the royal family
must find somewhere more secure.


01:42:51.700 --> 01:42:54.200
Metz is one of the strongest
fortresses in Europe.


01:42:54.400 --> 01:42:55.800
You will not be safe here.


01:42:55.900 --> 01:42:59.100
I will see to it that
my mistresses are off at once...


01:42:59.200 --> 01:43:01.800
...but my place is here
with my husband.


01:43:30.700 --> 01:43:32.200
Goodbye.


01:44:58.100 --> 01:45:01.100
Your Majesty, your immediate
return is requested.


01:45:01.200 --> 01:45:02.500
There's a mob of hundreds...


01:45:02.700 --> 01:45:05.800
...on their way in demand
of flour from their sovereign.


01:45:10.400 --> 01:45:12.600
It would be more secure
to decamp to Rambouillet...


01:45:12.700 --> 01:45:15.600
- ...twice the distance from Paris.
- I will not be a fugitive king.


01:45:15.600 --> 01:45:16.900
It is too dangerous here.


01:45:17.100 --> 01:45:18.700
At least send
the queen and children.


01:45:18.800 --> 01:45:21.300
My place is at the king's side.


01:45:21.700 --> 01:45:23.800
The first of them
have arrived in town.


01:45:23.900 --> 01:45:25.600
We will stay here.


01:45:47.600 --> 01:45:50.700
Save the queen, madame.
They're coming to kill her.


01:45:59.700 --> 01:46:02.300
Celine, don't be frightened.


01:46:02.300 --> 01:46:03.600
Let's get the children.


01:50:08.700 --> 01:50:11.300
Are you admiring your lime avenue?


01:50:14.700 --> 01:50:16.300
I'm saying goodbye.

